Project: Affinity Stone Rewards Merch Shop

Always reference SCOPE_OF_WORK.txt when working on features for this project.

Key Guidelines:
1. This is an MVP - prioritize simple, working solutions over complex features
2. Use Next.js 15 App Router with Server Components and Server Actions (avoid API routes unless necessary)
3. All admin write operations require authentication check via requireAdmin() helper
4. Always add isDevMode checks to prevent crashes when Supabase isn't configured
5. Use existing patterns from the codebase (check similar pages before implementing)
6. Revalidate affected routes after data mutations
7. Don't create .md files unless explicitly requested
8. When building features, implement in small, testable chunks that add immediate value
9. Use Windows 10 commands (PowerShell doesn't accept "&&")
10. Ignore all .md files unless explicitly referenced

Tech Stack:
- Next.js 15 (App Router)
- Supabase (auth + PostgreSQL with RLS)
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Server Components + Server Actions (prefer over client-side)
- pnpm workspaces (monorepo)

File Structure:
- apps/affinity-stone/ - Main Next.js app for Affinity Stone client
- packages/core/ - Shared UI components for all future clients
- Database migrations in apps/affinity-stone/supabase/migrations/

Development Mode:
- The app supports "dev mode" with placeholder Supabase credentials
- Check isDevMode with: !process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL || process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL.includes('placeholder')
- In dev mode, show mock data and disable write operations with clear messaging

Current Status: See Phase tracking in SCOPE_OF_WORK.txt
